  "preamble": "A coda nasal [n] after a front vowel can be lost while its nasality passes onto the vowel, so the result is a nasalized [ĩ]. In Portuguese, Latin and Old Galician-Portuguese -in lost its final nasal consonant, giving modern [ĩ], spelled -im.",
